    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We have a crisis with one of our cold-chain shipments. A refrigerated container carrying a large batch of tuna for the Tokyo market is having major issues. The cooling unit keeps cutting out intermittently, and we're seeing temperature spikes that threaten the entire load. \n\nWhat are the immediate protocols we should follow to protect the inventory and ensure we aren't violating food safety regulations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
