      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In the face of this cold-chain crisis, it's crucial to act swiftly and decisively, as the fate of your tuna batch hangs in the balance. First, you must immediately notify your logistics partner and the Tokyo market about the issue, ensuring transparency and maintaining trust. Next, assess the situation to determine if the cooling unit can be repaired or replaced on the spot, or if the shipment needs to be rerouted to a nearby facility with the necessary equipment.\n\nMeanwhile, consider using portable cooling units or ice packs to stabilize the temperature until a permanent solution is found. It's essential to document every step taken to mitigate the issue, as this will be crucial for compliance with food safety regulations. Remember, in the world of cold-chain logistics, a single misstep can lead to a cascade of problems, much like a single misstep by a mischievous goblin can lead to a whole village's misfortune. So, stay vigilant and proactive in your response to this crisis.",
